{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/data/story/index.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"shout:/[A-Z]{5}/.test(text)\\\",\\\"shout:/[A-Z]{5}|\"'^[A-Z]{2,}!/.test(text)\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('\"'src/view/materials.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"map:labelTexture(text,{color})\\\", \\\"map:labelTexture(text,{color,...(/\"'^'\"\\\\\\\\d{1,2}\"'$/.test(text)?{width:128,height:128,font:'\"'700 96px Barlow,sans-serif'}:{})})\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/view/entities.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\".075,.075,i?col.cyan:col.gold\\\", \\\".1,.1,i?col.cyan:col.gold\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/view/field.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"let kind='forearm',surface;\\\", \\\"let kind='forearm',surface,stavePainted=false;\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"function reset(next){kind=next;\\\", \\\"function reset(next){stavePainted=false;kind=next;\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"update(s){beat.value=\\\", \\\"update(s){if(\"'!stavePainted&&s.entities.some(e=>!e.done&&['\"'adagio','tremolo','legato','crescendo','fermata','coda','nest','note'].includes(e.kind))){stavePainted=true;ctx.strokeStyle='rgba(42,13,53,.3)';ctx.lineWidth=2.5;for(let i=0;i<5;i++){ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(140,440+i*24);ctx.bezierCurveTo(380,423+i*24,700,465+i*24,890,448+i*24);ctx.stroke();}texture.needsUpdate=true;}beat.value=\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/ui/ui.css');s=p.read_text()+'''\\\\n@media(min-height:900px) and (min-aspect-ratio:4/3){.objective-phase,.objective-tools,.tool-help,.bark-name,.gift-label,.syringe-button,.gift-button,.site-button,.target-label,.tray-label,.combo,.pause-chip,.bpm,.small,.eyebrow,.back-btn{font-size:2.125rem}.tool-help kbd{font-size:1.7rem;height:2rem}.tool-slot span{font-size:2.125rem;width:2.2rem;height:2.2rem;top:-.8rem;right:-.3rem}.tool-center small{font-size:1.8rem}}\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/browser/final-visuals.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"for(let i=0;i<7;i++)await page.locator('[data-action=advance]').evaluate(el=>el.click());\\\", \\\"while((await page.evaluate(()=>__game.state().storyLine))<3)await page.locator('[data-action=advance]').evaluate(el=>el.click());\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"await page.evaluate(()=>__game.test.idle(-600000));await page.waitForTimeout(wait);\\\", \\\"await page.evaluate(()=>{if(\"'!__game.test)throw Error(window.__renderError||'\"'render unavailable');__game.test.idle(-600000);});await page.waitForTimeout(wait);\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/data/about.json');import json;a=json.loads(p.read_text());a['testingFeedback'][0]='24 tracked issue groups fixed. Final suite: 94 checks. Viewport matrix: 19 clean screenshots.';a['testingFeedback'][1]='8 classified critical: phase interlocks, exhausted clamps, armless attacks, moved anchors, excessive regrowth, shared suture tearing, invalid trophy geometry, and out-of-range skinning indices.';p.write_text(json.dumps(a,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('docs/TESTING-NOTES.md');s=p.read_text().replace('22 tracked issue groups. Six','24 tracked issue groups. Eight');s+='''\\\\n23. **Critical:** extracted strain trophies lacked live guide data. Their render geometry now has safe defaults; a rendered post-extraction regression check keeps the following phase alive.\\\\n24. **Critical:** Float32 cylinder endpoints could generate a negative skinning index. Clamping the normalized skin position fixes the skeleton bounds; every strain is now drawn on WebGPU, WebGL2 and WebKit in the graphics checks.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/interview.mjs\nnpm run build\nnode tests/browser/final-visuals.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"agent_message","text":"The rendered-strain check caught a graphics-only bug: a cylinder endpoint could produce an invalid skinning index. It’s fixed, and the graphics tests now draw every strain on WebGPU, WebGL2, and WebKit. I’m reviewing those frames, then running the combined suite against the packaged HTML.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Code complete / final checks\n- Node suite now has 66 passing checks, including task scaling, exclusive grabs, synchronized shocks, feeder regeneration bounds, wrong-link regrowth and concurrent sutures.\n- Shared event presentation now gives Hub clients the same barks, grades, tool sounds and cut-ins as the host.\n- Extracted objects use actual Rapier poses for their arc, collision pile and landing clink.\n- Added a real offline file:// check of the root hand-in, plus a rendered extraction/trophy regression.\n- Rendered strain review found a real graphics-only crash: Float32 cylinder endpoints could create index −1/65535 in skin weights. Clamped normalized positions. The browser graphics cases now draw every strain on WebGPU, WebGL2 and WebKit.\n- Extracted strain trophies now have safe guide-geometry defaults.\n- Numbered stitch gates use square, readable label textures; musical staves paint onto infected organs; TV secondary type increased where appropriate.\n- Feedback ledger finalized at 24 tracked issue groups, 8 critical; see docs/TESTING-NOTES.md. About data and root exit-interview.json are filled in, Usage stays added on import.\n- Final expected combined count is 94 (66 sim + 21 browser + 7 hub). This is not yet the final executed combined result.\n- Final rendered visual sweep is running as exec session 15874. It writes artifacts/final-*.png. Earlier visual run failed before Adagio due the skin index issue; fixed and quick rendered Adagio now succeeds.\n- Development server still runs at http://127.0.0.1:37593 in owned exec session 26147; close it when finished.\n\n## Remaining finish steps\n1. Wait for final visual sweep, inspect images (especially characters, strains, cut-in, report, card). Fix only concrete findings.\n2. Run \"'`node tests/run-all.mjs` on the final build; ensure all checks pass. Final feedback currently says 94 checks, update if needed.\n3. Recheck changed short-screen UI through viewport matrix or screenshots; previous full matrix had 19 clean images.\n4. Check root exit-interview.json parses, final HTML matches dist/game.html, no unresolved markers. Update this progress log with final outcomes; stop owned server.\n5. Final response links the root HTML, exit JSON and dev docs, and includes all four required Source Information / Testing Feedback / Engine Feedback / Prompt Feedback blocks. Cite official Hub protocol if referencing research.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Code complete / final checks\n- Node suite now has 66 passing checks, including task scaling, exclusive grabs, synchronized shocks, feeder regeneration bounds, wrong-link regrowth and concurrent sutures.\n- Shared event presentation now gives Hub clients the same barks, grades, tool sounds and cut-ins as the host.\n- Extracted objects use actual Rapier poses for their arc, collision pile and landing clink.\n- Added a real offline file:// check of the root hand-in, plus a rendered extraction/trophy regression.\n- Rendered strain review found a real graphics-only crash: Float32 cylinder endpoints could create index −1/65535 in skin weights. Clamped normalized positions. The browser graphics cases now draw every strain on WebGPU, WebGL2 and WebKit.\n- Extracted strain trophies now have safe guide-geometry defaults.\n- Numbered stitch gates use square, readable label textures; musical staves paint onto infected organs; TV secondary type increased where appropriate.\n- Feedback ledger finalized at 24 tracked issue groups, 8 critical; see docs/TESTING-NOTES.md. About data and root exit-interview.json are filled in, Usage stays added on import.\n- Final expected combined count is 94 (66 sim + 21 browser + 7 hub). This is not yet the final executed combined result.\n- Final rendered visual sweep is running as exec session 15874. It writes artifacts/final-*.png. Earlier visual run failed before Adagio due the skin index issue; fixed and quick rendered Adagio now succeeds.\n- Development server still runs at http://127.0.0.1:37593 in owned exec session 26147; close it when finished.\n\n## Remaining finish steps\n1. Wait for final visual sweep, inspect images (especially characters, strains, cut-in, report, card). Fix only concrete findings.\n2. Run \"'`node tests/run-all.mjs` on the final build; ensure all checks pass. Final feedback currently says 94 checks, update if needed.\n3. Recheck changed short-screen UI through viewport matrix or screenshots; previous full matrix had 19 clean images.\n4. Check root exit-interview.json parses, final HTML matches dist/game.html, no unresolved markers. Update this progress log with final outcomes; stop owned server.\n5. Final response links the root HTML, exit JSON and dev docs, and includes all four required Source Information / Testing Feedback / Engine Feedback / Prompt Feedback blocks. Cite official Hub protocol if referencing research.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
